---
// The two reading views: the welcome pseudo-file (the works index) and the
// document view (header with rename, the preview body, the editor host).
---
<!-- welcome: the works index — the boot screen, a read-only pseudo-file
     (not editable, deliberately NOT a real file: a top-level file would
     take a number and pollute the user's works tree). The app notes
     under the index behave like notes.md: read-only, and hidden by the
     drafts toggle together with the drafts. -->
<div class="empty" id="empty">
  <div class="doc-col">
    <header class="doc-head"><h1>Welcome to I author</h1></header>
    <div class="md-body" id="empty-body"></div>
  </div>
</div>
<template id="welcome-notes">
  <div class="md-body toc-notes">
    <ul>
      <li><code>draft_</code> in a name = draft; the drafts toggle (the eye) hides drafts, notes, empty folders</li>
      <li><code>notes.md</code> = folder notes, takes no number; <code>prologue</code>, <code>epilogue</code>, <code>appendix</code> … print bare</li>
      <li>the hidden <code>NN_</code> prefixes only order — everything is numbered by position</li>
      <li>saves commit themselves; <code>ctrl/cmd+S</code> pushes now; unsynced text renders lighter until confirmed</li>
      <li>right-click the tree: new / delete · click a header title: rename · the corner title folds the tree, double-click goes home</li>
      <li><code>ctrl/cmd+click</code> opens links in the preview; the <em>pdf</em> button sets a text for print</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</template>
<article class="doc" id="doc" hidden>
  <!-- ONE centred column: the topline wraps it, the content rides its
       start — any inset change lands on .doc-col and the line follows -->
  <div class="doc-col">
    <header class="doc-head" title="click to edit the file name">
      <h1 id="doc-title"></h1>
      <input id="doc-rename" class="doc-rename" hidden autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" />
      <div class="doc-meta">
        <span class="chip" id="doc-draft" hidden>(draft)</span>
        <span class="chip" id="doc-words"></span>
        <button class="btn-tiny pdf-btn" id="pdf-toggle" hidden
                title="pdf — compile this scope, right-click for sizes">pdf</button>
      </div>
      <button class="measure-h measure-a" type="button" title="drag — page width (stays centred)"
              aria-label="drag to change the page width"></button>
      <button class="measure-h measure-b" type="button" title="drag — text width"
              aria-label="drag to change the text width"></button>
    </header>
    <div class="md-body" id="doc-body" hidden></div>
    <div id="editor-host" hidden></div>
  </div>
</article>
